      "caption_text": "🌸 “Flowers ask you to be present. They’re beautiful but fragile and impermanent, a reminder to slow down and notice the world around us.” We collaborated with artist @harukohayakawa (Haruko Hayakawa) to design her own take on the classic Instagram icon.\n\nHaruko is a NYC-based CG artist working across still life, product visualization, campaign art and editorial illustration. Her work explores the space between realism and surrealism, drawing on nature, materiality, heritage and belonging to transform familiar objects and symbols into something more immersive and unexpected.\n\n“I wanted the florals to feel integrated into the glyph rather than decorating its surface. I preserved the structure of the mark while introducing a sense of organic irregularity. Every detail had to support the silhouette and stay legible, even at the smallest scale. That tension between lushness and clarity became central to the piece.”\n\nHer icon “Garden Mode” is available now with Instagram Plus. Long-press the Instagram icon on your home screen to find it.",
